WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.232 --> 00:00:18.176
Sherlock gave his royal client a piercing look.

2
00:00:18.196 --> 00:00:23.798
"Are you sure that Irene Adler has not yet sent your photograph to the Scandinavian royal family?"

3
00:00:23.818 --> 00:00:25.799
"I am certain about that."

4
00:00:26.699 --> 00:00:29.000
The king of Bohemia nodded gravely to Holmes and me.

5
00:00:29.972 --> 00:00:33.754
"She said that she would send the photograph on the day the engagement was announced, and that will

6
00:00:33.794 --> 00:00:34.595
be next Monday."

7
00:00:34.615 --> 00:00:39.938
"Oh, then we have three days," said Holmes with a yawn.

8
00:00:39.958 --> 00:00:44.580
"That's fortunate because I have one or two other important cases right now.

9
00:00:45.521 --> 00:00:47.762
Your Majesty will, of course, remain in London?"

10
00:00:47.782 --> 00:00:53.265
"Certainly. You'll find me at the Langham Hotel under the name of Count Von Kramm.

11
00:00:54.226 --> 00:00:56.367
Let me know as soon as you have made any progress."

12
00:00:57.347 --> 00:00:58.108
The king sighed.

13
00:00:59.112 --> 00:01:01.534
"I would gladly surrender part of my kingdom for that photograph."

14
00:01:01.554 --> 00:01:06.078
"That's very well, but what should I use for expenses?"

15
00:01:06.539 --> 00:01:07.139
asked Holmes.

16
00:01:08.080 --> 00:01:10.142
The king laid a heavy cloth bag on the table.

17
00:01:10.162 --> 00:01:13.885
"Here are three-hundred pounds in gold and seven-hundred pounds in notes."

18
00:01:14.846 --> 00:01:16.868
Holmes then asked for Irene Adler's address.

19
00:01:16.888 --> 00:01:20.591
"I trust that we'll soon have some good news for you, Your Majesty."

20
00:01:21.552 --> 00:01:25.516
After the king left, Holmes said that we would discuss the case again tomorrow at three o'clock.

21
00:01:26.476 --> 00:01:30.780
The next afternoon I was in our rooms at Baker Street at three o'clock, but Holmes had not

22
00:01:30.820 --> 00:01:31.440
yet returned.

23
00:01:32.361 --> 00:01:33.282
Our landlady, Mrs.

24
00:01:33.322 --> 00:01:36.544
Hudson, informed me that he had left the house at eight o'clock that morning.

25
00:01:37.525 --> 00:01:39.346
I sat down by the fire to wait for him.

26
00:01:40.347 --> 00:01:45.331
It was almost four o'clock when a disheveled stable groom with a red face and side-whiskers entered the

27
00:01:45.371 --> 00:01:51.196
room. I was used to my friend's amazing powers of disguise, but I still had to look three

28
00:01:51.256 --> 00:01:52.837
times to be sure it was Holmes.

29
00:01:53.818 --> 00:01:58.574
He vanished into his bedroom and soon returned, looking as respectable as ever in a tweed suit.

30
00:01:59.554 --> 00:02:02.096
Taking a seat by the fire, he dissolved into laughter.

31
00:02:02.116 --> 00:02:04.778
"Well, really!"

32
00:02:05.098 --> 00:02:05.919
he finally said.

33
00:02:05.939 --> 00:02:07.420
"What is it?"

34
00:02:07.840 --> 00:02:08.240
I asked.

35
00:02:08.260 --> 00:02:10.001
"It's too funny.

36
00:02:11.002 --> 00:02:13.003
I'm sure you'll never guess how I spent my morning."

37
00:02:13.023 --> 00:02:15.745
"I suppose you've been out to Miss Adler's house."

38
00:02:16.746 --> 00:02:19.908
"Quite so, but what happened afterward was rather unusual."

39
00:02:20.888 --> 00:02:26.012
Disguised as an unemployed stable groom, Holmes had quickly found Miss Adler's house, Briony Lodge.

40
00:02:27.048 --> 00:02:31.051
Although there was a large walled garden at the back, the front of the house was close to

41
00:02:31.091 --> 00:02:31.491
the road.

42
00:02:33.272 --> 00:02:37.915
From the street, it was easy to see into the spacious, well-furnished sitting room on the ground floor.

43
00:02:38.935 --> 00:02:43.838
"I wandered down the street," said Holmes, "and found a stable in a lane that runs alongside the

44
00:02:43.878 --> 00:02:47.800
garden. I lent the stablemen a hand in rubbing down their horses.

45
00:02:48.801 --> 00:02:54.148
In return I received a few coins, some tobacco, and more information than I could use about Miss

46
00:02:54.249 --> 00:02:56.971
Adler and half a dozen other neighbors that I didn't care about."

47
00:02:56.991 --> 00:02:59.553
"And what did they say about Irene Adler?"

48
00:02:59.913 --> 00:03:00.313
I asked.

49
00:03:00.333 --> 00:03:05.397
"She is the daintiest thing under a bonnet, according to every man there," said Holmes.

50
00:03:06.438 --> 00:03:12.243
"She lives quietly, sings at concerts, drives out at five every day, and returns at seven sharp for

51
00:03:12.283 --> 00:03:16.226
dinner. She has only one male visitor, but sees a great deal of him.

52
00:03:17.927 --> 00:03:18.668
He is Mr.

53
00:03:18.748 --> 00:03:23.372
Godfrey Norton, a dark and handsome lawyer, who calls once a day and sometimes twice."

54
00:03:24.444 --> 00:03:28.666
After Holmes had heard everything the men had to tell, he began to walk up and down near

55
00:03:28.706 --> 00:03:30.748
Briony Lodge while he thought over his plan.

56
00:03:30.768 --> 00:03:36.811
"I realized that this Godfrey Norton was evidently an important factor in the matter," Holmes said to me.

57
00:03:36.831 --> 00:03:39.812
"The fact that he was a lawyer sounded ominous.

58
00:03:40.853 --> 00:03:44.755
What was his relationship with Miss Adler and what was the object of his repeated visits?

59
00:03:45.736 --> 00:03:48.497
Was she his client, his friend or his mistress?

60
00:03:49.598 --> 00:03:53.860
If she was a client, she had probably already transferred the photograph to him for safekeeping."

61
00:03:54.764 --> 00:03:59.145
While Holmes was trying to decide whether to remain at Briony Lodge or to visit the gentleman's office,

62
00:03:59.765 --> 00:04:02.066
a hansom cab arrived and a man sprang out.

63
00:04:03.786 --> 00:04:08.188
Holmes noted that he was a dark and remarkably handsome man, and so assumed that he was Godfrey

64
00:04:08.228 --> 00:04:13.669
Norton. "He appeared to be in a great hurry, shouted to the cabman to wait, and brushed past

65
00:04:13.709 --> 00:04:15.810
the maid who opened the door," said Holmes.

66
00:04:15.830 --> 00:04:21.491
"I caught glimpses of him through the sitting-room window, pacing up and down, waving his arms, and talking

67
00:04:21.571 --> 00:04:24.472
excitedly. I saw nothing of Miss Adler."

68
00:04:25.444 --> 00:04:28.727
Soon Norton emerged from the house, looking even more agitated than before.

69
00:04:29.808 --> 00:04:33.551
As he approached the cab, he pulled a gold watch from his pocket and glanced at it.

70
00:04:33.571 --> 00:04:36.474
"Drive as fast as you can to the Church of St.

71
00:04:36.514 --> 00:04:38.235
Monica!" he shouted to the cabdriver.

72
00:04:38.255 --> 00:04:41.318
"I'll give you half a pound if you do it in twenty minutes!"

73
00:04:42.439 --> 00:04:45.582
Holmes was just wondering if he should follow when a carriage came up the lane.

74
00:04:47.243 --> 00:04:49.465
The coachman was still struggling into his coat.

75
00:04:49.485 --> 00:04:55.102
"As soon as it pulled up," said Holmes, "Irene Adler shot out the front door and into the

76
00:04:55.142 --> 00:05:00.047
carriage. As it drove away, I heard her promise the coachman half a pound if he could reach

77
00:05:00.087 --> 00:05:01.588
St. Monica's in twenty minutes."

78
00:05:02.609 --> 00:05:06.412
Holmes knew that he should go in pursuit of them, and luckily a cab came down the street.

79
00:05:06.432 --> 00:05:11.757
"The driver looked twice at such a shabby fare, but I jumped in before he could object," said

80
00:05:11.797 --> 00:05:16.161
Holmes. "It was twenty-five minutes before noon, and I suspected what was happening."

81
00:05:17.081 --> 00:05:18.042
When Holmes reached St.

82
00:05:18.082 --> 00:05:19.744
Monica's, he hurried into the church.

83
00:05:20.840 --> 00:05:25.543
In front of the altar stood the couple and a clergyman, who seemed to be vigorously scolding them.

84
00:05:26.584 --> 00:05:30.786
Holmes slunk up the aisle like any other unemployed person who had wandered into a church.

85
00:05:32.547 --> 00:05:36.469
Suddenly the three people turned around, and Godfrey Norton came running up to Holmes.

86
00:05:37.470 --> 00:05:38.010
"Thank God!"

87
00:05:38.311 --> 00:05:38.751
he cried.

88
00:05:38.771 --> 00:05:39.411
"You'll do.

89
00:05:39.631 --> 00:05:40.492
Come! Come!"

90
00:05:40.512 --> 00:05:42.213
"What do you mean?"

91
00:05:42.613 --> 00:05:43.193
asked Holmes.

92
00:05:43.213 --> 00:05:44.574
"Come, man!

93
00:05:45.455 --> 00:05:47.216
We only have three minutes, or it won't be legal."

94
00:05:48.156 --> 00:05:52.878
Norton dragged Holmes to the altar, where my friend found himself muttering responses that were whispered in his

95
00:05:52.978 --> 00:05:56.180
ear and assisting in the marriage of Irene Adler to Godfrey Norton.

96
00:05:56.200 --> 00:05:59.742
"It was all finished in an instant," Holmes said to me.

97
00:05:59.762 --> 00:06:04.524
"And then there was the gentleman thanking me on one side, and the lady on the other side

98
00:06:04.564 --> 00:06:06.325
while the clergyman beamed in front of us.

99
00:06:07.466 --> 00:06:12.188
It was the most preposterous situation I've ever been in, and that's why I was laughing just now."

100
00:06:13.884 --> 00:06:18.146
Apparently the couple had needed to marry by noon or their marriage license would not be valid.

101
00:06:19.067 --> 00:06:23.129
But the clergyman had refused to marry them without a witness, so they called on Holmes for help.

102
00:06:24.230 --> 00:06:29.112
After the ceremony, Holmes was surprised to see them go their separate ways, the lawyer to his office

103
00:06:29.412 --> 00:06:30.653
and the lady to her house.

104
00:06:31.674 --> 00:06:32.334
"What's next?"

105
00:06:32.774 --> 00:06:33.154
I asked.

106
00:06:33.174 --> 00:06:35.496
"You don't mind breaking the law?"

107
00:06:35.836 --> 00:06:36.456
Holmes asked.

108
00:06:37.457 --> 00:06:39.037
"Not in the least," I replied.

109
00:06:39.057 --> 00:06:41.619
"Nor risking a chance of arrest?"

110
00:06:42.599 --> 00:06:43.560
"Not for a good cause."

111
00:06:44.700 --> 00:06:48.625
"Then you are the man for the job that we will undertake later tonight," said Holmes.

112
00:06:49.666 --> 00:06:51.348
And with that he called for supper.
